{"assessments":[{"id":"2d9c069b6cc4","problem":true,"type":"prose","severity":1,"why":"The phrase 'seeded arithmetic fixture' is copied from the packet's software-testing vocabulary and is not explained. Applied management researchers may not know it means synthetic, code-generated data. The point is accurate and relevant, but stating plainly that the data are synthetic would be clearer."},{"id":"43584c2f522d","problem":false,"type":"none","severity":0,"why":"This is a short topic sentence for the caveats section. The next sentences immediately name the specific limitations (no random assignment, no concurrent control, confounders), so it is not vague in context and suits a director-facing email."},{"id":"2da0e3c3f706","problem":false,"type":"none","severity":0,"why":"The arithmetic is correct: 67 × $32 = $2,144, and $1,000 + $544 = $1,544, so the net is +$600. The terse equation format suits slide text."},{"id":"5cfcb34ba10c","problem":false,"type":"none","severity":0,"why":"This is an appropriate hook for a web article. It previews the finding that the gains look good but the net value is negative (−$600), which the article supports with correct figures."}]}
